@model GuidePageViewModel
@* QE@@Home: welcome section. Edit content here; layout, navigation and footer are in Views/Shared/_QEatHomeLayout.cshtml. *@
  <div class="hero"><div class="hero-img" style="background-image:url(/qe-at-home/img/entrance.jpg);background-position:50% 45%"></div>
    <div class="in">
      <div class="kicker">Academic Year 2026 to 2027</div>
      <h1>Distance Learning Guide</h1>
      <p>How learning, wellbeing and communication will work if the school moves to distance learning.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Welcome from the Principal</h2>
        <p>I hope this is a guide you never need. Our strong preference is always to have our students learning together in school. Given the current situation in the region, however, it is right that we plan carefully, so that if the UAE authorities or the KHDA direct schools to move to distance learning, every family knows exactly what to expect from the very first morning.</p>
        <p>This guide brings together the plans each phase of the school has prepared: how the school day will run, which platforms we will use, how QE Flourish and our Elevate inclusion support will continue, and how we will keep every child safe online. It also sets out what we will need from you, because distance learning works best when school and home work closely together.</p>
        <p>If we do move to distance learning, I will write to the whole community straight away, and I will send a weekly update for as long as it continues.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:1.4em"><strong>Mr Dan Clark</strong><br><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--gold);font-size:18px">Principal, Queen Elizabeth’s School, Dubai Sports City</span></p>
      </div>
      <img class="photo tall" src="/qe-at-home/img/principal.jpg" alt="Mr Dan Clark, Principal" style="max-width:380px;justify-self:center">
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="quote">Our aim is for remote learning to feel unmistakably QE: academically ambitious, purposeful and engaging, while grounded in relationships, care, character and a strong sense of belonging.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="center narrow"><h2>When Distance Learning Applies</h2>
        <p class="lead">The UAE may activate distance learning nationwide or for defined periods, and the KHDA may direct private schools in Dubai to move to distance learning. In either case, schools must maintain continuity of learning and student wellbeing.</p></div>
      <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:36px">
        <div class="card"><h3>System-wide activation</h3><p>When the UAE authorities or the KHDA mandate distance learning, we activate full remote provision, as described in this guide, for the shortest period possible.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Individual absences</h3><p>Remote learning is not offered when a child is absent for a short period, for example through illness. We will provide work to complete where appropriate, and monitor it.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>How you will hear</h3><p>The Principal will tell the whole community promptly, through our routine channels including email and social media. Each phase then shares the details for day one.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="center narrow"><h2>Our Principles</h2><p class="lead">Our approach follows the National Distance Learning Guidance (2025 to 2026). All of our safeguarding, wellbeing, inclusion and behaviour policies apply exactly as they do in school.</p></div>
      <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:36px">
        <div class="card"><h3>Continuity of Learning</h3><p>Essential curriculum learning continues.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Holistic Wellbeing</h3><p>Protecting physical, emotional and social health.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Partnership with Families</h3><p>Clear communication and guidance for learning at home.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Quality First</h3><p>Remote learning must be meaningful, ambitious and age appropriate.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Inclusion</h3><p>Students of Determination receive appropriate adjustments.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Safeguarding Online</h3><p>Online learning follows the same protection standards as learning on site.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="center narrow"><h2>Find Your Child’s Phase</h2></div>
      <div class="grid3 phase-cards" style="margin-top:32px">
        <a href="/qe-at-home/pre-prep"><img src="/qe-at-home/img/pp_wave.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:50% 60%"><div class="t"><h3>Pre-Prep</h3><p>Nursery, Pre-Prep One and Pre-Prep Two</p></div></a>
        <a href="/qe-at-home/prep"><img src="/qe-at-home/img/prep13.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:50% 65%"><div class="t"><h3>Prep School</h3><p>Years 1 to 6</p></div></a>
        <a href="/qe-at-home/senior"><img src="/qe-at-home/img/reader23.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:50% 32%"><div class="t"><h3>Senior School</h3><p>Years 7 and 8</p></div></a>
      </div>
      <p class="center" style="margin-top:36px"><a class="btn" href="/qe-at-home/contacts#checklist">Before day one: family checklist</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
